    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-29T09:17:54+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-29T09:17:54+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-28T23:47:54Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-28T23:47:54Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred to the northeast of Tasmania extends a ridge over the southeast of the continent. This high and ridge will move eastwards over the Tasman Sea in coming days. A series of slow moving troughs will enter the west of the state today then move across the state on Wednesday and Thursday as a couple of cold fronts will move across waters to the south. A new high pressure system will become established south of the Bight during Friday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW009" description="Flinders" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-29T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-28T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Winds northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h turning northerly 25 to 40 km/h in the morning then decreasing to 20 to 30 km/h in the late afternoon. Daytime maximum temperatures 31 to 36.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">No Rating</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 8:50am to 3:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-30T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-29T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower near the coast in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Winds northwest to northeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending northwesterly in the middle of the day then tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h in the late evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-10-01T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-30T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Very high chance of showers, most likely in the afternoon and evening. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds northwest to northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending westerly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning then turning south to southwesterly during the day. Overnight temperatures falling to between 15 and 20 with daytime temperatures reaching 24 to 31.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-10-02T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-10-03T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-10-01T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-10-02T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Slight chance of a shower in the morning. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Hawker in the morning. Mostly sunny afternoon. Winds south to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 8 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
